{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487246-the-hecata-in-fall-of-london","id":1487246,"title":"The Hecata in Fall of London","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T13:38:40-07:00","id":1487246,"title":"The Hecata in Fall of London","content":"Kind of a silly question, but I wondered about it.<br /> <br /> In the Fall of London chronicle, one of the preset character is a Hecata. However, he awakes at the start of the adventure after being in Torpor since 1941, when Hecata didn't really exist. So he must have identified himself with one of the various groups coalescing into the Hecata.<br /> <br /> Put aside the question on what he was back then (he doesn't really fit any of the standard groups, and doesn't belong to the Giovanni family, at least by name or by Sire), how does it work for a vampire that suddenly comes back like that? wouldn't he be confused? wouldn't he find himself with totally different Disciplines or different Clan banes from the original ones? I'm mentioning it because the book doesn't even touch the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> (speaking of Fall of London, isn't it a pity that there's not even a small section on how was London in 1941 when the characters fall asleep? it could have been a nice source for roleplaying)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27082-perles75","name":"Perles75","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T14:46:52-07:00","id":1487254,"title":"","content":"I think officially the Hecata were created with a Necromantic ritual that affected everyone in the World of Darkness using the blood of Augustus Giovanni.<br /> <br /> So he'd wake up a Hecata and wonder how the Hell he no longer causes pain with his fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T16:18:02-07:00","id":1487269,"title":"","content":"Haven't the PCs in <i>Fall of London</i> lost their memories? So if Henry had a different weakness before, he might not know it. As for his disciplines, Hecata have the three Cappadocian disciplines by default. Henry and his sire sound like generic Hecata, in which case they would have the same disciplines, but God knows how they survived before the Sixth Great Maelstrom. If they're related to Pater Thomas, they would have those disciplines, but I don't know which clan bane he's supposed to have. He says that he has trouble physically writing in <i>Camarilla</i>, which could be the Cappadocian bane, but he doesn't seem like that in later books.<br /> <br /> I think Henry is an example of the sort of kindred that the developers wanted to make playable by writing the Hecata, i.e. a modern Cappadocian (mostly) without the constraints of the surviving bloodlines' backgrounds; it just doesn't make sense for a character of that age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T20:08:03-07:00","id":1487307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487246-the-hecata-in-fall-of-london?p=1487254#post1487254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think officially the Hecata were created with a Necromantic ritual that affected everyone in the World of Darkness using the blood of Augustus Giovanni.<br /> <br /> So he'd wake up a Hecata and wonder how the Hell he no longer causes pain with his fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought the Hecata <b><i>did</i></b> cause pain with their fangs. Didn't Lamia's Kiss replace all the other weaknesses of the non-Giovanni bloodlines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T03:45:45-07:00","id":1487564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487246-the-hecata-in-fall-of-london?p=1487269#post1487269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't the PCs in <i>Fall of London</i> lost their memories? So if Henry had a different weakness before, he might not know it. As for his disciplines, Hecata have the three Cappadocian disciplines by default. Henry and his sire sound like generic Hecata, in which case they would have the same disciplines, but God knows how they survived before the Sixth Great Maelstrom. If they're related to Pater Thomas, they would have those disciplines, but I don't know which clan bane he's supposed to have. He says that he has trouble physically writing in <i>Camarilla</i>, which could be the Cappadocian bane, but he doesn't seem like that in later books.<br /> <br /> I think Henry is an example of the sort of kindred that the developers wanted to make playable by writing the Hecata, i.e. a modern Cappadocian (mostly) without the constraints of the surviving bloodlines' backgrounds; it just doesn't make sense for a character of that age.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that was my main issue... regardless of mechanical questions, which can be circumvented by &quot;magic! you have now these powers&quot; I was thinking more of the roleplay aspect of it. Even if the character might experience some memory lapses, there is still the question that in the sheet there's written &quot;Hecata&quot; which is something he would not identify with (also, he can't really be Cappadocian, can he? I know they've tried to retcon it, but they've basically been exterminated. He can't be Giovanni either, so he must belong to a secondary bloodline, but nothing really fits the brief of his character. Unless he comes from the line of de Camden, which is strange in itself because de Camden has largely kept a low profile to avoid problems and it doesn't fit the idea of him creating childer grandchilds?).<br /> <br /> So it's something thats not easy to convey to the player without some blunder (&quot;erm yes, your clan is Hecata -which actually doesn't ring a bell to you because it didn't exist when you fell asleep? But you don't exactly remember what you were before so let's go with that!&quot;). I was wondering if there was a more elegant solution, roleplay-wise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27082-perles75","name":"Perles75","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}